    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter the September 14 slate with a clear focal point in **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, whose elite sprint speed and favorable matchup against L\u00f3pez yield a team-high score of 80.98. His placement in the leadoff spot, paired with a solid 0.371 xwOBA, makes him an indispensable anchor as we hunt stolen bases, the scarcest resource in our Roto race. **Lars Nootbaar** also grades out as a strong play at 65.16, benefiting from a prime leadoff position and a 13% boost from his favorable matchup against Alcantara. Meanwhile, **Carson Benge** cracks the 60-threshold (61.14), leveraging a platoon advantage and the protection of the cleanup spot to provide reliable production despite facing Young.\n\nThe decision to bench **Chase Meidroth** was the most difficult call of the day, as he finished with a 33.18 score, falling well short of our 40-point floor. While **Chase Meidroth** offers upside, the elite pitching profile of Williams (2.89 xERA) severely suppressed his expectation, and his lower spot in the order further diminished his run-production potential. Elsewhere, the roster remains thinned by the absence of **Junior Caminero**, **Trea Turner**, and **Christian Yelich**, who are all sidelined by team off-days. We are proceeding with **Dillon Dingler**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Josh Smith**, and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** in our primary slots; however, these players remain marginal starts, as each faces a RHP matchup that tempers their scoring potential. We will monitor weather reports closely, though no acute risks currently threaten the viability of the **Dillon Dingler** or **Josh Smith** matchups.",
